skill-security-scan — Security Inspector Skill for Claude Code

This skill (`skill-security-scan`) vendors and adapts the threat taxonomy,
scoring model, and MCP/YARA pattern descriptions from NVIDIA SkillSpector
(https://github.com/NVIDIA/SkillSpector), licensed under Apache-2.0.

  Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All rights reserved.
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

This is a derivative, LLM-first reimplementation of the SkillSpector detection
taxonomy. It is NOT a redistribution of the SkillSpector source code. Pattern
IDs (P1-P8, E1-E4, PE1-PE3, SC1-SC6, EA1-EA4, OH1-OH3, MP1-MP3, TM1-TM3,
RA1-RA2, TR1-TR3, TP1-TP4, LP1-LP4, TT1-TT5, AST1-AST8, YR1-YR4) are
reproduced verbatim for interoperability. Explanations and remediations are
adapted from DEFAULT_EXPLANATIONS and DEFAULT_REMEDIATIONS in
`src/skillspector/nodes/analyzers/pattern_defaults.py`.

YARA rule textual signatures adapted from NVIDIA SkillSpector YARA rules
(`src/skillspector/yara_rules/`), which are in turn based on patterns from
Neo23x0/signature-base and community threat intelligence.

Taxonomy snapshot: SkillSpector pattern_defaults.py as of 2026-06-01.

Research basis: "Agent Skills in the Wild: An Empirical Study of Security
Vulnerabilities at Scale" (Liu et al., 2026). Dataset: 42,447 skills;
26.1% contain vulnerabilities; 5.2% show likely malicious intent.

